    "narrative": "For our July 7th slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (66.51) and **Taylor Ward** (64.16) stand as our primary offensive anchors. **Perdomo** benefits from a massive situational boost facing Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez, whose 5.64 xERA provides a significant floor-raising matchup, while the projected #2 spot in the order maximizes his run-scoring potential. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** capitalizes on favorable park factors (+16% boost) and a strong platoon advantage against Matthew Boyd. While **Gavin Sheets** (63.22) trails slightly, his ability to leverage a strong lineup position (#4) against Zac Gallen\u2019s 4.98 xERA makes him a high-upside play that rounds out the elite tier of our daily starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Dylan Beavers** (46.81), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Jeremiah Jackson**. While both players face the same Matthew Boyd matchup and share the same 33% rain risk, **Jeremiah Jackson** was ultimately preferred due to his batting order assignment and specific park-driven efficiency. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with the **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Taylor Ward** spots due to that non-trivial precipitation risk in their respective games. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 landscape.\n\nDespite the relative scarcity of stolen base opportunities, we are banking on the high-contact profiles of players like **Tyler Freeman** and **Daulton Varsho**, who are positioned to exploit specific pitcher delivery traits that favor aggressive baserunning. We have opted to bench **Lawrence Butler** (41.85) entirely today, as the matchup against a premier arm like Tarik Skubal (2.74 xERA) creates an efficiency floor too low for our aggressive pursuit of the categories. The remaining roster, including **Luis Arraez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Bryson Stott**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Jonathan Aranda**, maintains a steady, if marginal, expectation profile designed to protect our game caps while awaiting more favorable pitcher-opponent conditions later in the week.",
